; TH:Re8.1.IIb, a sitting item: one insight into a culture from an unseen described scene, with its evidence; TH:Cr2.1.IIb, the kept team interpretation sheet; TH:Cr3.1.IIa, a look-for on the production: a concept or design change made from rehearsal; TH:Pr6.1.IIa, a look-for: the production shaped for its chosen audience. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: devising on a global issue (Level 3). Tools: team interpretation sheet, artist statement, Curio Class's own. Free path: printed scripts, found costume pieces. Short path: 22 days | Last in Level 2, same slot as unit 5, because the production draws on every earlier Level 2 unit and ends the level; the year-end check follows in week 32 | Candidate: a Native American storytelling-theater company's own teaching, for range | The Dilemma of a Ghost: the sensitivity agent reads Aidoo's own published words and Ghanaian theater sources first; the play's family and its talk of childlessness are studied, not performed, and no student plays a Ghanaian or African American character by an accent. The company's blended forms are studied in its own words; no student imitates a Philippine dance or song. Beliefs: a public or invented option marked the same. A showing outside class needs a yes. Hazards and controls: as unit 5. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
