ial and historical reading; TH:Cr1.1.IIIa, a look-for on the concept portfolio: forms, conventions and technology blended; TH:Cr2.1.IIIa, a look-for: an original play idea with its research and two credited traditions, and a sitting item: whether an unseen described production borrows fairly, with reasons. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: the student's own production concept (Level 4). Tools: concept portfolio, source critique card, Curio Class's own. Free path: printed scenes. Short path: 17 days | Same slot as units 2 and 7; Advanced work starts from a concept the student sets, which every later Level 3 unit uses | Candidate: a director from Africa or Latin America as the second style, for range | Macbeth's killings are spoken, never staged as contact or with any weapon (mimed or a word). Kathakali and Kabuki: the sensitivity agent reads UNESCO's Kabuki page, a Kerala Kathakali institution's own page and published criticism of Les Atrides first; no student wears makeup, mask or costume of either tradition. The borrowing question is studied with care for the communities named. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
