ribed scene that uses a cultural or setting insight; TH:Cr2.1.IIIb, the kept ensemble choices sheet; TH:Cr3.1.IIIa, a look-for on the production: a style, genre and form chosen and kept; TH:Pr6.1.IIIa, a look-for: research from two roles visible in the production for its audience. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: the student-led production (Level 4). Tools: devising cards, ensemble choices sheet, artist statement, Curio Class's own; Curio Class writes the Fuenteovejuna scenes in English. Free path: printed scripts, found objects. Short path: 22 days | Last in Level 3, same slot as units 5 and 10; the devised production uses every Level 3 unit and ends the level, with the year-end check in week 32 | Candidate: the global issues offered on the problem card, checked for range and for none that asks a student to speak for their own community | Fuenteovejuna's commander abuses village women and is killed by the village: the unit stages the village's council and its "Fuenteovejuna did it" answers, never the abuse or the killing. The global issue: no student is cast to speak for a culture or community, their own or another; invented viewpoints are offered and marked the same. A showing outside class needs a yes (the student's own at 18 or over). Hazards and controls: as unit 5. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
