.1.IIb, a look-for: a revised choice traced to research or script study; TH:Cr1.1.IIc, a look-for on the file: a choice drawn from experience or knowledge (the student's own or an invented person's, marked the same); TH:Re7.1.IIa, a sitting item: two readings of a criterion applied to an unseen scene, with the next choice each would steer; TH:Re8.1.IIa, a kept response with proof and a stated standard; TH:Re8.1.IIc, a sitting item: three tastes in a set of unseen audience responses sorted and debated. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: defended techniques from sources (Level 3). Tools: character file, audience journal, Curio Class's own. Free path: printed scenes, found props. Short path: 17 days | Same slot as unit 3; after unit 7 because the character file uses checked research and a concept; before unit 9, whose critique uses the standards built here | Candidate: a character-comedy tradition from Asia or Africa beside Plautus and Moli�re | Sweat: a factory town's job losses, drug use and a violent assault; studied from a description of its choices, never performed, with a content note to students and families; the sensitivity agent reads the playwright's and a theater's pages first. Personal experience is invited, never required. Health's steps if a student tells something. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
